### TITLE ###
SpaceAndTabBothToggle
### DESCRIPTION ###
Two keys toggle the cursor row, so a user who reaches for either gets the same
result.
### PROMPT ###
Pick
### OPTIONS ###
a
b
c
### KEYS ###
space
down
tab
enter
### SELECTED ###
a
b
### FRAMES ###
--- frame 0 (initial) ---
Pick
> [ ] a
  [ ] b
  [ ] c
--- frame 1 (space) ---
Pick
> [x] a
  [ ] b
  [ ] c
--- frame 2 (down) ---
Pick
  [x] a
> [ ] b
  [ ] c
--- frame 3 (tab) ---
Pick
  [x] a
> [x] b
  [ ] c
--- frame 4 (enter) ---
Pick a, b

### TITLE ###
TogglingAcrossTheList
### DESCRIPTION ###
Navigating between toggles leaves the untouched rows alone.
### PROMPT ###
Pick
### OPTIONS ###
o1
o2
o3
o4
o5
### KEYS ###
down
space
down
down
space
enter
### SELECTED ###
o2
o4
### FRAMES ###
--- frame 0 (initial) ---
Pick
> [ ] o1
  [ ] o2
  [ ] o3
  [ ] o4
  [ ] o5
--- frame 1 (down) ---
Pick
  [ ] o1
> [ ] o2
  [ ] o3
  [ ] o4
  [ ] o5
--- frame 2 (space) ---
Pick
  [ ] o1
> [x] o2
  [ ] o3
  [ ] o4
  [ ] o5
--- frame 3 (down) ---
Pick
  [ ] o1
  [x] o2
> [ ] o3
  [ ] o4
  [ ] o5
--- frame 4 (down) ---
Pick
  [ ] o1
  [x] o2
  [ ] o3
> [ ] o4
  [ ] o5
--- frame 5 (space) ---
Pick
  [ ] o1
  [x] o2
  [ ] o3
> [x] o4
  [ ] o5
--- frame 6 (enter) ---
Pick o2, o4

### TITLE ###
SelectedComesBackInOptionOrder
### DESCRIPTION ###
Toggling c before a still reports [a, c]: the result is ordered by the option
list, not by when each was chosen.
### PROMPT ###
Pick
### OPTIONS ###
a
b
c
### KEYS ###
down
down
space
home
space
enter
### SELECTED ###
a
c
### FRAMES ###
--- frame 0 (initial) ---
Pick
> [ ] a
  [ ] b
  [ ] c
--- frame 1 (down) ---
Pick
  [ ] a
> [ ] b
  [ ] c
--- frame 2 (down) ---
Pick
  [ ] a
  [ ] b
> [ ] c
--- frame 3 (space) ---
Pick
  [ ] a
  [ ] b
> [x] c
--- frame 4 (home) ---
Pick
> [ ] a
  [ ] b
  [x] c
--- frame 5 (space) ---
Pick
> [x] a
  [ ] b
  [x] c
--- frame 6 (enter) ---
Pick a, c

### TITLE ###
CheckboxRendering
### DESCRIPTION ###
The cursor marker and the checkbox are separate: a row can be under the cursor
without being selected, which is what makes the two-column prefix worth
rendering at all.
### PROMPT ###
Pick
### OPTIONS ###
a
b
### KEYS ###
space
enter
### SELECTED ###
a
### FRAMES ###
--- frame 0 (initial) ---
Pick
> [ ] a
  [ ] b
--- frame 1 (space) ---
Pick
> [x] a
  [ ] b
--- frame 2 (enter) ---
Pick a

### TITLE ###
CancelLeavesNoSummary
### DESCRIPTION ###
Ctrl-C discards the selection, and the last frame is the interactive render
rather than a summary claiming something was chosen.
### PROMPT ###
Pick
### OPTIONS ###
a
b
### KEYS ###
space
ctrl-c
### SELECTED ###
<canceled>
### FRAMES ###
--- frame 0 (initial) ---
Pick
> [ ] a
  [ ] b
--- frame 1 (space) ---
Pick
> [x] a
  [ ] b
